From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Liu <admin@ob-buff.dev>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 22:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nfnetlink: seed missing records from refresh dumps

nlbwmon normally inserts records from conntrack multicast events and only
updates existing records while processing periodic conntrack dumps. If the
kernel does not deliver those multicast events, a new database stays empty
even though the conntrack dump contains active flows.

Insert a record when a refresh update reports that it does not exist yet.
Keep the update-only behavior for existing records so periodic refreshes do
not inflate connection counts.

Signed-off-by: Felix Liu <admin@ob-buff.dev>
---
--- a/nfnetlink.c
+++ b/nfnetlink.c
@@ -80,6 +80,21 @@ database_insert_immediately(struct record *r)
 {
-	if (r->count != 0)
-		database_insert(gdbh, r);
-	else
-		database_update(gdbh, r);
+	int err;
+
+	if (r->count != 0) {
+		database_insert(gdbh, r);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	err = database_update(gdbh, r);
+
+	/*
+	 * Conntrack multicast events can be unavailable on some recent kernels.
+	 * In that case the periodic dump is the first time a flow is observed.
+	 * Seed the missing record here, while preserving update-only behaviour
+	 * for records which already exist so connection counts do not inflate.
+	 */
+	if (err == -ENOENT) {
+		r->count = htobe64(1);
+		database_insert(gdbh, r);
+	}
 }
